Z||000000||GeeDee86GT||11-05-2000||10:19 PM||||Just closed the deal on my first Fiero. An 86 SE (4spd). I've got red eyes for reading all the posts here.  FANTASTIC!  I have lots of work to do over the winter so I'm sure to ask lots of questions. Like: If I make a center section removable in the back window, will I get fume problems(no sunroof, fumes bad... noise good)  Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>Gary <BR>86 SE work in progress <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/garby_d" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/garby_d</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||11-05-2000||10:30 PM||||The Fiero is designed to have a vacuum right behind the rear window, to help draw hot air out of the vents. Creating a removable window here would hinder this effect, if not prevent it completely.<BR>V8-Archie had a removable window like this on his blue chop top, so there's a chance it doesn't cause any major problems. I suggest you talk to him (www.v8archie.com) about this, to see if he encountered any problems etc.<P>anyway, welcome to the forum..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>where exactly is Almonte? I've never heard of it..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
